course: dictionary
lesson: 7307
title: The pituitary gland
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word can be hard, but its context tells you what it means. In «Long bones grow at soft growth plates near their ends, told to work by hormones from the pea-sized pituitary gland under the brain», the clues are pea-sized and under the brain. So the pituitary gland is a small gland, about the size of a pea, sitting under the brain.
explain: Pituitary is an adjective here. It describes the gland, as in «pituitary hormones». People often shorten it to a noun and say «the pituitary», which means the pituitary gland.
explain: A gland makes chemicals and releases them into the body. Those chemicals are hormones, and they are messengers. The pituitary gland sends hormones that tell other parts of the body what to do, and its hormones control growth.
fact: The pituitary gland is a small gland, about the size of a pea, under the brain.
fact: «Pituitary» is an adjective in phrases like «pituitary hormones», meaning belonging to the pituitary gland.
fact: The pituitary gland is often called the master gland because it tells other glands what to do.
fact: Growth hormone from the pituitary gland affects how tall a person grows.
fact: «Growth plates» are soft areas near the ends of long bones, where the bone grows longer; when they harden in the late teens, a person stops getting taller.
exercise: Where is the pituitary gland? In «the pea-sized pituitary gland under the brain», the clue is under the brain. | *Under the brain | On the skin | Inside the heart | In the foot
exercise: What size is the pituitary gland? | As big as a football | As big as a house | *About the size of a pea | Bigger than the brain
exercise: In the phrase «pituitary hormones», which word is the adjective? | *pituitary | the | hormones | gland
test: Why is the pituitary gland called the master gland? | Because it is the biggest gland in the body | Because it makes food | Because it sits on top of the heart | *Because it tells other glands what to do
test: What does the pituitary gland control? | *Growth and many other body processes | Only your fingernails | Only your eyesight | Only the colour of your hair
exam: In «When the plates harden in the late teens, a person stops getting taller», what tells the growth plates to work? | *Hormones from the pituitary gland | Cold weather | Sunlight on the skin | Only sleep at night
